Z||000018||Reality||10-28-2001||09:43 PM||||Does anyone still have the picture of that black thing from florida last year that had the carbon fiber wing on it? And By the BY that wing is huge on a Fiero actually it's huge on anything I have seen it on several different domestic and import cars. The second wing dosen't look oh so bad on a Fiero once it's molded in but again as it's been stated the fiero basically performs better without a wing/spoiler. The last one is just an ugly thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> the end caps are too small an those little bumps just look like tumors on it! And not to stir up the mustang bunch but if yeah big wings might consider this one: <A HREF="http://www.spoilers.com/images/spoilers1/mustang760rw.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.spoilers.com/images/spoilers1/mustang760rw.jpg</A> <BR>I saw it on a V-8 Fiero and it just seem to fit the car totally Makes viewing out the back a pain in the arse but hey who knows? I mean to each their own. Personally I had a 61" aluminum touring wing on my car and everyone around here loved it. But I decided to go ahead and put a stock wing on, trust me nothing looks better than the orginal, mainly because nothing else was desinged for the car. Okat that my rant||||reg||1
Z||000019||Nashco||10-28-2001||10:17 PM||||Just because you guys have no imagination doesn't mean you should slam the post...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://home1.gte.net/jbnash/88weclipsespoiler.jpg"> <BR>This guy had a little more imaginitive thinking, and came up with something that I think fits the Fiero well.<P>I came across this pic somehow a while ago, and saved it to my hard drive I liked it so much.  It's an aftermarket wing for an eclipse that has been modified to fit the fiero.  If you look at the second link posted above, it's not too far from that design.  I think this wing looks excellent.  For a long time I was thinking of doing this, but eventually decided against it.  I like the look of the stock wing, and it's the perfect width, so I'm using it.  I'm going to make some 12" stantions for it, with some built in adjustment.  At this height it will actually be USEFUL, and yes, I do plan on hitting 120...often as I can get the chance to.  I want to make this car become a weekend warrior (racecar) but still a daily driver.  Some of us like certain styles, some of us have ambitions, some of us think a little differently.  Don't slam that; sure, if you're hanging out with your buddies and they feel the same way, that's fine...but this is a pretty diverse forum, and you never know what may become of things.  &lt;/RANT&gt;<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000020||GTDusty||10-28-2001||10:41 PM|||| I was actually wondering if I should get an aluminum spoiler like the imports had on F&F. I happened to get GT3 for my PS2 and loved the look of the aluminum spoiler on the 30th annv. Lotus Espirit; and since the Fiero is similar in styling..me thinks it would look good on my GT too!!!! <P> Dusty<P>BTW: 'Rice' as its known in the import world are modifications that add no performance whatsoever to your car despite your claims. i.e. Type-R stickers on a stock car, tons of vinyl for products not on your car, 'dial-in' numbers shoe-polished on your car window that you pulled out of your arse.<P>||||reg||4
